{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773097567,"nonce":"HkxrVJYci1jjCxTsipzCMhV7tR0=","title":"auth-merge: kickstart -k races with storeExecutionResult — background restart with delay","message":"restart_mandible_if_dist_changed() in cli/auth-merge.sh calls launchctl kickstart -k synchronously while still running as a child of the executor. This sends SIGTERM to the daemon before storeExecutionResult() can run, producing \"daemon killed mid-execution\" on every merge that touches dist/. Fix: background the kickstart with a 3s sleep so auth-merge.sh exits first, the executor records the result, then the daemon restarts. Confirmed as root cause of all 20+ stuck-request recoveries at each startup.","files":null}]}